Z||000009||MinnGreenGT||12-24-2001||11:08 AM||||Yup! Winter has finally arrived- and I got my Fiero into storage just in time (it actually had about 1/2inch of that slush/snow stuff on it when we finally pulled it into my Dad's PoleShed. I've got pics of it wedged in between my Dad's 88GT and my brother's '79 Porsche 924 with only about 7 inches on either side!<P>Oh well, the first and probably last time I'll ever get to drive the Fiero up until December 22nd!  I'm just praying for a short winter and a long nice spring.<P>EDIT: oh yeah, it's about 10 degrees outside right now (10:15am) with a windchill of about -10 degrees. High today... a balmy 15 degrees and the windchill will probably never go positive!<P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 12-24-2001).]||||reg||1
